{"path":"chrono/weekday/operator_cmp","title":"std::chrono::operator==(std::chrono::weekday)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::</span>operator==<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::chrono::weekday)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/weekday/operator_cmp","section":"chrono","kind":"page","summary":"Compare the two std::chrono::weekday x and y.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/chrono\">&lt;chrono&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">==</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2576\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">weekday</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2576\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">weekday</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Compare the two <span class=\"t-lc\">std::chrono::weekday</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y</span></code>.\n</p><p>The <code>!=</code> operator is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/default_comparisons#Other_defaulted_comparison_operators\">synthesized</a> from <code>operator==</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x.<span class=\"me1\">c_encoding</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> y.<span class=\"me1\">c_encoding</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><code>weekday</code> does not support the <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code> and <code>&gt;=</code> operators because there is no universal consensus on which day is the first day of the week.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;chrono&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">literals</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2576\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">weekday</span></span></a> wd1<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2576\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">weekday</span></span></a> wd2<span class=\"br0\">{</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2581\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">Friday</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>wd1 <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> wd2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// 13 January 1313 is a Friday</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/weekday\"><span class=\"kw2576\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">weekday</span></span></a> wd3<span class=\"br0\">{</span>1313y<span class=\"sy2\">/</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"sy2\">/</span>13d<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>wd2 <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> wd3<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/weekday","title":"std::chrono::weekday"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::operator==(std::chrono::weekday)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Compare the two std::chrono::weekday x and y."},{"label":"Return value","note":"x.c_encoding() == y.c_encoding()"},{"label":"Notes","note":"weekday does not support the <, <=, > and >= operators because there is no universal consensus on which day is the first day of the week."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":96,"codeBlockCount":1}
